P(X = 1) = \frac{^{3}C_1 \times ^{15}C_1}{^{18}C_2} = \frac{3 \times 15}{153} = \frac{45}{153}
P(X = 2) = \frac{^{3}C_2}{^{18}C_2} = \frac{3}{153}
Now, calculate the Expected Value \(E(X)\):
E(X) = 0 \times P(X=0) + 1 \times P(X=1) + 2 \times P(X=2)
E(X) = 0 \times \frac{105}{153} + 1 \times \frac{45}{153} + 2 \times \frac{3}{153}
E(X) = \frac{45 + 6}{153} = \frac{51}{153} = \frac{1}{3}
Next, calculate \(E(X^2)\):
