Finally, calculate the Variance \(Var(X)\):
Var(X) = E(X^2) - (E(X))^2
Var(X) = \frac{57}{153} - \left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^2
Var(X) = \frac{57}{153} - \frac{1}{9}
To subtract, find a common denominator. Since \(153 = 9 \times 17\), we can write \(\frac{1}{9} = \frac{17}{153}\).
Var(X) = \frac{57}{153} - \frac{17}{153}
Var(X) = \frac{57 - 17}{153} = \frac{40}{153}

